  "comments": "<p>This New Zealand definitive two dollar coin was first issued into circulation in 1999 &amp; also in BU and Proof sets with the obverse featuring Ian Rank-Broadley's fourth portrait of Queen Elizabeth II. These coins have been minted at various different Mints over the years. From 2010 The $1 BU &amp; Proof set coins (Except for the Unofficial BU Sets of 2014 &amp; 2015 which were struck at the Royal Mint) were minted at the Royal Dutch Mint and are made from Brass instead of Aluminium-bronze.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The Kotuku is one of New Zealand's rarest birds and held in high regard in Maori mythology.&nbsp;</p>",
